# ds-mirror.env — single source of truth for the host-local git mirror.
#
# Every other file in images/mirror/ reads these values:
#   - mirror.sh / smoke.sh source this file (DS_MIRROR_ROOT, DS_MIRROR_PORT, ...)
#   - the systemd refresh unit pulls it in via EnvironmentFile= (mirror.sh then
#     reads DS_MIRROR_ROOT at runtime)
#   - the quadlet pulls it in via EnvironmentFile= so the CGI runtime env is set,
#     but note: quadlet's own keys (Image=, PublishPort=, Volume=) are read by
#     the quadlet GENERATOR, not the container runtime, so they CANNOT expand
#     EnvironmentFile vars — those literals (image, 127.0.0.1:8418, /var/lib/
#     ds-mirror -> /srv/git) are kept in lockstep with the values here BY HAND.
#     Change a value here and you must change the matching literal in
#     ds-mirror-serve.container too.
# Within those limits, paths and ports never drift across the tree.
#
# This file holds NO secrets. The mirror holds no long-lived upstream
# credentials of its own: mirror-to-upstream fetch rides the boundary
# credential-swap path (egress gateway / ds-tlsproxy, D83; doc 16 §5).

# Where bare --mirror clones live on the host.
DS_MIRROR_ROOT=/var/lib/ds-mirror

# Read-only serve face (git-http-backend). Host-loopback only — VMs reach it on
# their host-local gateway address, never the public internet.
DS_MIRROR_ADDR=127.0.0.1
DS_MIRROR_PORT=8418

# Container image for the stock git-http-backend serve face (no code we wrote).
# Digest-pinned (tag@sha256, see images/README.md): the tag stays human-readable,
# the digest binds. This is the canonical reference value; the quadlet's Image=
# literal (a generator key, not runtime env) must be edited to match it byte-for-
# byte by hand — see the EnvironmentFile note above. lint-env-drift.sh enforces it.
DS_MIRROR_IMAGE=docker.io/alpine/git:latest@sha256:4a0e72d49596a1f5d3701aeedafdadc5c0da4062be4657c7bdc4017387f591cc
